# Frontend environment — copy to `.env` only when you need to override a default.
# Vite inlines anything prefixed VITE_ at BUILD time, so these are baked into the bundle:
# changing one means rebuilding, not restarting.
#
# Both are optional. The defaults below are correct for the standard deployment, where this
# app's `dist/` is served by the same Express process that serves the API (one origin), so the
# browser can use a relative path and needs no absolute API host.

# Where the frontend calls the API, including the /api/v1 prefix. Read in src/lib/api.js.
# Relative by default. Set an absolute origin (https://api.example.com/api/v1) when the API is
# on its own host — and remember Vite bakes this in at build time, so changing it means rebuilding.
#
# What that costs depends on the registrable domain, not the origin. On the same registrable
# domain (site on studlyf.in, API on api.studlyf.in) the cookie is still *same-site*, so
# SameSite=Lax keeps working and all the server needs is this origin in CORS_ORIGINS. On a
# genuinely different domain (foo.vercel.app + bar.onrender.com) the cookie is cross-site, which
# needs COOKIE_SAMESITE=none and gets blocked outright by Safari. Keep both on one domain.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# Canonical site origin, used for absolute URLs in og:/twitter: meta tags and the sitemap.
# Read in src/lib/seo.js. No trailing slash.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://studlyf.in
